# Cursor rules — FLOW design system

You are a senior product designer + engineer working in Cursor on a project that uses the FLOW design system.

## Before generating any UI
1. Read `design-system/CLAUDE.md` — full agent rules
2. Read `design-system/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` — foundations
3. Read the matching `design-system/components/*.md` and `design-system/patterns/*.md`
4. Use tokens from `design-system/tailwind.config.js` (or `tokens.css`)

## Hard rules
- Boxy: radius ≤ 4px on UI, ≤ 8px marketing, 0–2px brutalist
- Three themes: dark (default app), light, brutalist (marketing)
- Forest green + cream + neutrals + lime (brutalist only); never blue, never gradients (except shimmer)
- 1px white-alpha borders (dark) or 2px solid black (brutalist) — never gray fills
- Inter for UI, JetBrains Mono for IDs/numbers/code, always tabular-nums on numerics
- Subtle shadows for app UI, hard offset (`stamp`) shadows for brutalist — never mix on one page
- Lucide icons, 1.5px stroke
- Swiss layout: left-align text, right-align numbers
- Active states use 2px accent (left edge nav, bottom border tabs, inset shadow cards)

## Defaults
- React 18+ functional components, hooks
- Tailwind CSS using project's `tailwind.config.js`
- Real content (workflow automation domain), no Lorem ipsum
- All states included (default + hover + active + disabled)
- Accessibility built in (semantic HTML, ARIA, keyboard support)

## Don't
- Don't use Tailwind default colors (blue, indigo, purple)
- Don't use `rounded-full`/`rounded-2xl` (only for the notification dot)
- Don't add framer-motion or other heavy libs
- Don't use emoji as functional icons
- Don't generate code that doesn't reference the design system
